LOSSES=['C53 current Finding Definition/source-use admission,C12 accepted normalization planning,retained prototype scaffold and C70 flat Finding carrier remain separate from translation-owner fidelity.','Normalized semantic.finding/type.definition/scope.knowledge-development belongs to DefinitionContext,not a grant of canonical Definition or decision authority to a Finding record.','Finding denotes a declared evidence-bounded attributable conclusion;bound Research investigation is preserved in separate referenced ResearchContext rather than making Finding itself Research or an aggregate.','A Finding derives from one-or-more explicit ResearchRun or EvidenceSet bases;those descriptive basis labels and ResearchContext maps require accepted concrete Run/Set identities and directional correspondence.','Finding question equals each referenced ResearchContext question;the source target does not independently supply this field,so the accepted target/source Question and Scope projection remains pending.','Claim wording not exceeding support is a declared WordingWithinSupport relation between separately typed Wording and SupportBound;no opaque-string order or actual adequacy theorem is invented.','ResearchContext preserves Project,one-or-more Goals,method,sources/observations,support/counterevidence,limitations,Finding references,created/updated and owner/challenge routes. There are no current Goal/Project Definition identities.','Research.outcome absence,Research-not-Finding and the source exclusions of silently promoted aggregate conclusions apply to ResearchContext. Separate ResearchActualOutcome queries preserve those exact source boundaries without erasing the Finding target conclusion genus.','Finding and referenced Research Context limitations and explicit challenge routes preserve declaration structure without proving practical challengeability or owner authority.','Source/provenance,wording/support,Question/Scope,temporal and route handles do not authenticate actual investigation,source currentness,origin,adequacy,truth or acceptance.','Required collection declarations do not force every ResearchContext membership or Finding limitations collection nonempty;the source target requires one-or-more derivation bases and those are independently enforced.','Research supporting and counterevidence membership may overlap;Finding truth and claimed support-state labels remain independent outcomes.','Finding and Research Context exclude aggregate/decision/Definition/policy/proof/execution roles as applicable;promotion declarations do not establish actual authority and actual independently supported outcomes are not denied.','D61 split source does not merge Finding,EvidenceSet,ResearchInquiry or ResearchRun identities;declared sibling assignments need explicit nonempty sibling refs,but actual adoption and Typed Relations remain separate.','Created/updated research refs are independent and un-ordered;ephemeral Research declarations do not introduce retention/deletion behavior or the richer flat carrier revision lifecycle as source axioms.','Current Finding carrier requires Run refs and Set refs simultaneously,concrete support assessment and lifecycle/revision fields. Full source correspondence,universal mandatory support interpretation and accepted consumer mappings remain unresolved.','Exact selected local D61 H2 recovery and source-use admission do not authenticate live producer repository identity/currentness or establish source-owner fidelity and whole-definition proof.']
